  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Counting principles and probability describe and predict uncertain outcomes.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Counting &amp; probability",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Permutations \\( {}_nP_r=\\tfrac{n!}{(n-r)!} \\); combinations \\( {}_nC_r=\\tfrac{n!}{r!\\,(n-r)!} \\). Probability \\( =\\tfrac{\\text{favourable}}{\\text{total}} \\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Factorial",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( n! \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Permutation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{n!}{(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Combination",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Probability",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\tfrac{\\text{fav}}{\\text{total}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 11.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Compute \\( {}_5C_2 \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{5!}{2!\\,3!}=10. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Normal distribution application",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Heights are normally distributed with \\(\\mu=170\\) cm and \\(\\sigma=10\\) cm. Find the probability that a randomly chosen person has height between 160 and 185 cm.</p>\\[P(160\\leq X\\leq185)=P(-1\\leq Z\\leq1.5)=\\Phi(1.5)-\\Phi(-1)=0.9332-0.1587=0.7745.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "In a class of 200 students taking a test with mean 65 and SD 12 (normally distributed), how many students would you expect to score above 80?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(P(X>80)=P(Z>1.25)=1-0.8944=0.1056\\). Expected: \\(200\\times0.1056\\approx21\\) students.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
